@startuml
allowmixing
title 5G Telco Style: CP vs UP + NGFW/SASE Service Chain (Renderer-Safe)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam roundcorner 20
skinparam padding 10
skinparam nodesep 50
skinparam ranksep 55
left to right direction

' ============================================================
' Lane 1: UE + RAN
' ============================================================
rectangle "UE + NG-RAN" as L1 {
  rectangle "UE" as UE
  rectangle "gNB\n(5G Base Station)" as GNB
}

' ============================================================
' Lane 2: 5GC Control Plane
' ============================================================
rectangle "5GC — Control Plane" as L2 {
  rectangle "PCF\nPolicy Control" as PCF
  rectangle "SMF\nSession Mgmt" as SMF
}

' ============================================================
' Lane 3: 5GC User Plane
' ============================================================
rectangle "5GC — User Plane" as L3 {
  rectangle "UPF\nUser Plane Function" as UPF
}

' ============================================================
' Lane 4: Security Service Chain
' ============================================================
rectangle "Security Service Chain" as L4 {
  rectangle "NGFW / SASE\n(DPI, IPS/IDS,\nURL Filtering,\nThreat Intel,\nTelemetry)" as NGFW
}

' ============================================================
' Lane 5: Data Network
' ============================================================
rectangle "Data Network (DN)" as L5 {
  rectangle "Internet / Enterprise DN" as DN
}

' ============================================================
' Hidden alignment edges (avoid overlap)
' ============================================================
UE -[hidden]-> GNB
GNB -[hidden]-> PCF
PCF -[hidden]-> SMF
SMF -[hidden]-> UPF
UPF -[hidden]-> NGFW
NGFW -[hidden]-> DN

' ============================================================
' User Plane
' ============================================================
UE --> GNB : 5G NR Air\n(User traffic)

GNB --> UPF : N3 (GTP-U)\nUser plane packets
UPF --> NGFW : N6 Steering\n(service chain / redirect)
NGFW --> DN : Forward clean traffic

UPF ..> DN : N6 Direct\n(Bypass)\n(optional)

' ============================================================
' Control Plane
' ============================================================
PCF --> SMF : Npcf\nPolicy + QoS + steering intent
SMF --> UPF : N4 (PFCP)\nInstall rules:\nPDR/FAR/QER/URR

' ============================================================
' Notes
' ============================================================
note right of UPF
UPF applies rules:
- PDR: match flow
- FAR: forward/redirect/drop
- QER: QoS enforcement
- URR: usage report
end note

note bottom
Two modes:
1) Full inline: all traffic -> NGFW/SASE
2) Selective steering: only risky flows -> NGFW/SASE,
   rest bypasses to keep latency low.
end note

@enduml
